  m_Text: 'Map lunar craters using a SAR Radar. Eclipse lasts 45% of each orbit,
    and a transmitter overheat occurs on Orbit 2.


    FLIGHT ADVISORY: Extended
    lunar eclipse windows cut solar generation nearly in half each pass. Pair high-capacity
    Li-Ion storage with thermal/TX autopilot rules.


    OPERATIONS: Equip a RADAR
    payload, verify mass & power margins in the Hangar, and configure A.S.T.R.A.
    autopilot before launch.'
